  "originalText": "Practice Test\n\nConvert the improper fraction to a mixed number.\n\n672.\n\n\\(\\frac{19}{5}\\)\n\nConvert the mixed number to an improper fraction.\n\n673.\n\n\\(3\\frac{2}{7}\\)\n\nLocate the numbers on a number line.\n\n674.\n\n\\(\\frac{1}{2},1\\frac{2}{3},−2\\frac{3}{4},\\) and \\(\\frac{9}{4}\\)\n\nIn the following exercises, simplify.\n\n675.\n\n\\(\\frac{5}{20}\\)\n\n676.\n\n\\(\\frac{18r}{27s}\\)\n\n677.\n\n\\(\\frac{1}{3}·\\frac{3}{4}\\)\n\n678.\n\n\\(\\frac{3}{5}·15\\)\n\n679.\n\n\\(−36u(−\\frac{4}{9})\\)\n\n680.\n\n\\(−5\\frac{7}{12}·4\\frac{4}{11}\\)\n\n681.\n\n\\(−\\frac{5}{6}÷\\frac{5}{12}\\)\n\n682.\n\n\\(\\frac{7}{11}÷(−\\frac{7}{11})\\)\n\n683.\n\n\\(\\frac{9a}{10}÷\\frac{15a}{8}\\)\n\n684.\n\n\\(−6\\frac{2}{5}÷4\\)\n\n685.\n\n\\((−15\\frac{5}{6})÷(−3\\frac{1}{6})\\)\n\n686.\n\n\\(\\frac{−6}{\\frac{6}{11}}\\)\n\n687.\n\n\\(\\frac{ \\frac{p}{2} }{ \\frac{q}{5} }\\)\n\n688.\n\n\\(\\frac{−\\frac{4}{15}}{−2\\frac{2}{3}}\\)\n\n689.\n\n\\(\\frac{{9}^{2}−{4}^{2}}{9−4}\\)\n\n690.\n\n\\(\\frac{2}{d}+\\frac{9}{d}\\)\n\n691.\n\n\\(−\\frac{3}{13}+(−\\frac{4}{13})\\)\n\n692.\n\n\\(−\\frac{22}{25}+\\frac{9}{40}\\)\n\n693.\n\n\\(\\frac{2}{5}+(−\\frac{7}{5})\\)\n\n694.\n\n\\(−\\frac{3}{10}+(−\\frac{5}{8})\\)\n\n695.\n\n\\(−\\frac{3}{4}÷\\frac{x}{3}\\)\n\n696.\n\n\\(\\frac{{2}^{3}−{2}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}}\\)\n\n697.\n\n\\(\\frac{\\frac{5}{14}+\\frac{1}{8}}{\\frac{9}{56}}\\)\n\nEvaluate.\n\n698.\n\n\\(x+\\frac{1}{3}\\) when\n\n1. ⓐ\\(x=\\frac{2}{3}\\)\n\n2. ⓑ\\(x=−\\frac{5}{6}\\)\n\nIn the following exercises, solve the equation.\n\n699.\n\n\\(y+\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{7}{5}\\)\n\n700.\n\n\\(a−\\frac{3}{10}=−\\frac{9}{10}\\)\n\n701.\n\n\\(f+(−\\frac{2}{3})=\\frac{5}{12}\\)\n\n702.\n\n\\(\\frac{m}{−2}=−16\\)\n\n703.\n\n\\(−\\frac{2}{3}c=18\\)\n\n704.\n\nTranslate and solve: The quotient of \\(p\\) and \\(−4\\) is \\(−8.\\) Solve for \\(p.\\)\n\n4.10.2: Practice Test is shared under a CC BY  4.0  license and was authored, remixed, and/or curated 